1
00:00:00,869 --> 00:00:03,789
...and Dr. Winkle just ripped
the sign-up sheet off the wall.

2
00:00:03,955 --> 00:00:06,375
It wasn't an official sign-up sheet.
He printed it...

3
00:00:06,541 --> 00:00:10,041
(Leslie:)...and he put his name down
on every slot for the next six months.

4
00:00:10,211 --> 00:00:12,801
(Sheldon:)If it is a crime to ensure
the university's resources...

5
00:00:12,964 --> 00:00:15,754
(Sheldon:)...are not being squandered
chasing subatomic wild geese...

6
00:00:15,925 --> 00:00:17,595
(Sheldon:)...then I plead guilty.

7
00:00:17,761 --> 00:00:19,431
[PHONE RINGING]

8
00:00:20,972 --> 00:00:22,052
(Sheldon:)Oh, Penny.

9
00:00:22,223 --> 00:00:25,013
- You need to get that, Dr. Cooper?
- God, no.

10
00:00:25,185 --> 00:00:27,855
(Leslie:)Don't turn it off. You might miss
your call from Nobel...

11
00:00:28,021 --> 00:00:31,731
(Leslie:)...letting you know you've been nominated
as dumb-ass laureate of the year.

12
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:36,283
(Sheldon:)Oh, yeah, well,
you wouldn't even be nominated.

13
00:00:41,493 --> 00:00:45,243
I have a series of important multi-loop
calculations and simulations to run.

14
00:00:45,413 --> 00:00:47,373
She's reducing irrelevant data,
making a mock...

15
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:48,580
[PHONE RINGS]

16
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:50,210
(Gablehauser(as phone rings):)Excuse me.

17
00:00:50,377 --> 00:00:52,337
(Scene:)Gablehauser.

18
00:00:53,546 --> 00:00:58,026
(Gablehauser(as phone rings):)It's for you.

